<description>
Count each colored object's enclosed black pixels and pack those counts into a 3x3 summary.

Input structure
- A black background contains exactly two 4-connected monochrome foreground objects arranged left-to-right.
- Each foreground object encloses one or more black pixels inside its bounding box.

Rule
- Count, for each object, the black pixels inside its bounding box that are not 4-connected to the bounding-box border through black pixels.
- In left-to-right object order, allocate enough 3-wide output rows for that count and fill that many cells left-to-right with the object's color.

Key insight
- The output is not the hole shapes themselves; it is a compact row-packed count summary of the enclosed background area of each object.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "two 4-connected monochrome foreground objects ordered left-to-right",
  "dst": "3-wide output row blocks ordered top-to-bottom",
  "match_cond": "left-to-right rank of s == top-to-bottom rank of d",
  "transform": "count each object's enclosed black pixels not 4-connected to its bbox border, then fill that many cells left-to-right in its row block with the object color",
  "grid_shape": "fixed 3x3 summary grid"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: fixed 4 rows x 9 cols, black background
  objects:
    count: exactly 2 monochrome 4-connected foreground objects, distinct non-black colors
    arrangement: left-to-right, column-separated by >=0 all-black columns (gap 0-4 [observed])
    bbox_isolation: each object's bbox contains only its color and black (no overlap between bboxes)
    bbox_size: 3-5 rows x 3-5 cols [observed]
    shape: |
      single 4-connected component forming a closed loop that encloses >=1 black pixel.
      Most are rectangular frames (all bbox-border cells colored); some are irregular
      with 1-2 bg cells on bbox border and 1-2 colored cells in interior, but still
      enclosing >=1 pixel by flood-fill from bbox border.
    enclosed_bg: 1-6 black pixels not 4-reachable from bbox border through black
  output_constraint: |
    3x3 grid. For each object (left then right), pack enclosed_bg_count cells
    with its color left-to-right row-by-row into consecutive 3-wide rows.
    ceil(enc_left/3) + ceil(enc_right/3) <= 3.
    Total enclosed across both objects: 2-7 [observed].

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick two distinct non-black colors c1, c2
    - Choose enc1 in 1..6 and enc2 in 1..6 such that ceil(enc1/3)+ceil(enc2/3) <= 3
    - Build the 3x3 output by packing enc1 cells of c1 then enc2 cells of c2 left-to-right
    - For each object, build a closed-loop shape on a 4-row canvas that encloses exactly enc_i black pixels (simplest approach is a rectangular frame of appropriate interior size; for variety, occasionally create irregular frames by removing 1-2 border cells and adding interior cells while preserving the enclosed count via flood-fill check)
    - Place left object, then >=1 black separator column, then right object; pad with black columns to reach width 9
```
